[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      184[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    offset-3/7 patterns and 6 seeds, so the branch is verified by hash equality
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      185[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    rather than by hitting it. Confirmed computationally unreachable, not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      186[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    overlooked.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      187[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Which `string.mode` `sh_geti` picks on each of its two passes.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      188[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `SH_STRDUP` and `SH_ARENA` produce byte-identical stdout (the printed key
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      189[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    *contents* and value do not depend on where the key is stored), and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      190[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `sh_geti` returns `void` and frees everything. Swapping the two modes inside
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `sh_geti` is therefore invisible from outside. The *behaviour* of each mode
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    is still verified directly via `stbds_shmode_func` plus a full
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    put/get/del/free cycle (rows 24–26, 37–39, 45–48, 50).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
